\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Global policy entropy}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{entropy}

\p{For a rollout law induced by #{\pi}, define the \strong{global policy
entropy} over a horizon #{T} by}

##{
  \mathcal H_{\mathrm{glob}}(\pi)
  =\mathbb E\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}
    H\bigl(\pi_t(\cdot\mid H_t)\bigr)\right],
  \qquad
  H(p)=-\sum_a p(a)\log p(a).
}

\p{The finite entropy formula comes from \citet{Pt. I, Sec. 6}{shannon1948mathematical}.
The name and finite-horizon aggregation are an FTIP specialization. The
displayed quantity applies conditional entropy to the policy's visited
histories. It depends on the task and environment law, even when that
dependence is suppressed from the notation.}

\p{RLVR papers use entropy for several different statistics. DAPO reports
entropy dynamics under its policy and sampling procedure
\citef{yu2025dapo}. The global quantity above must not be substituted for a
token-specific covariance or selected-action surprisal.}
